{"id": "EUVD-2026-103050", "enisaUuid": "50ec5516-7cd9-3275-8200-8c2d98c92c4a", "description": "10up Distributor before 2.3.2 contains a PHP object injection vulnerability that allows Contributor-level users to instantiate PHP objects by double unserializing distributed post meta. Attackers can store a serialized PHP string as meta, which set_meta() in includes/utils.php unserializes on the destination site, storing attacker-defined objects whose impact depends on loaded gadget classes.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:39:02", "baseScore": 2.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/10up/distributor/security/advisories/GHSA-wm53-9j85-ph6h", "https://github.com/10up/distributor/blob/2.3.1/includes/utils.php#L192-L200", "https://github.com/10up/distributor/commit/7c57edb774d80534885ca6f2c46b95d333de6e5a", "https://github.com/10up/distributor/releases/tag/2.3.2", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/10up-distributor-before-2.3.2-php-object-injection-via-set-meta"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111628", "GHSA-p88q-h74f-qxvq"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.27, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "5b21c891-283d-3e4e-a0ed-b411a36ec613", "product": {"name": "Distributor", "vendor": {"name": "10up"}}, "product_version": "0 <2.3.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0d4f86d8-49d0-3e34-b1ad-b229951db2c9", "vendor": {"name": "10up"}}], "isExploited": false}